WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.680
We have been hearing more and&nbsp;
more over the last several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:09.360
weeks to a month and a half or so. Republicans&nbsp;
and right wing media pushing the narrative of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:17.440
a crisis at the border and a surge in undocumented&nbsp;
crossings. Last week, we covered House Minority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:24.160
Leader Republican Congressman Kevin McCarthy,&nbsp;
who staged an event at the US Mexico border,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:31.040
said unaccompanied minors are coming to the U.S.&nbsp;
in crisis levels and the crisis was caused by Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.960
Biden. Kevin McCarthy said that terrorists are&nbsp;
coming in through the US Mexico border border&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:44.240
from Yemen, Turkey and Yemen, Turkey and Iran.&nbsp;
It was there was no actual evidence of that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.320
But this is the narrative. It's been pushed&nbsp;
by Fox News reporters during press briefings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.720
that's been pushed in news reports. It's been&nbsp;
pushed by Republicans at press conferences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.760
Is this real? Well, The Washington Post&nbsp;
analyzed Border Patrol data going back to 2012,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:07.280
and there appears to be no crisis whatsoever.&nbsp;
There is no surge that we could link to Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:13.920
administration policy. What we are seeing is data&nbsp;
that tracks a seasonal pattern. This is the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.760
of year where there are more migrants attempting&nbsp;
to cross and interacting with Border Patrol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:27.120
plus some what we might call pent up demand from&nbsp;
the covid period last year when movement was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:32.800
dramatically reduced. So if we look at a chart of&nbsp;
encounters per month at the border, looking at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.840
last few years and we're putting that up on the&nbsp;
screen, what you see is that numbers went up at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:43.760
exactly this time of year in twenty nineteen. They&nbsp;
did not in twenty twenty because of the pandemic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:49.280
They went up slightly at this time in twenty&nbsp;
eighteen. And that's the pattern. It's a pattern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.600
that's been observed for some time now. Yes.&nbsp;
Apprehended migrants are up twenty eight percent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.600 --> 00:02:01.840
from January to February, but apprehended migrants&nbsp;
were up 31 percent during the same period in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:08.240
twenty nineteen. It is true that the raw numbers&nbsp;
are higher right now than last year and the year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:14.560
before. Remember, movement in general went down&nbsp;
during the pandemic. So what you are seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.840
number one right now is a resumption of movement.&nbsp;
And number two, some backed up demand from people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.400
who did not move around last year. Now, let me&nbsp;
be very clear, because I know I'm going to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.640
emails about this. I'm not saying we don't need&nbsp;
total and complete immigration reform. We do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.400
This doesn't mean that Joe Biden has done&nbsp;
enough to stop deportations. He hasn't,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.440
and I've talked about that. It simply is not the&nbsp;
crisis that Republicans want you to think it is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:47.280
It's the crisis that we've had in this country for&nbsp;
a long time, combined with a lack of comprehensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.400
immigration reform, which I and others have been&nbsp;
calling for for just as long of a time. What Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.400 --> 00:03:00.480
did last year with Title 42, which is using&nbsp;
the pandemic as a reason to turn people around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:07.040
and deport, it seems to have delayed people&nbsp;
from coming, not stopped people from coming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.560
period. That's the story. Many of them are&nbsp;
coming now, not because Joe Biden is president,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:18.480
but because the pandemic is to some degree easing,&nbsp;
almost identical to Joe Biden's surge in gas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:24.800
prices last week, which we covered earlier this&nbsp;
week. We are seeing gas prices go up. It's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.280
because of Joe Biden. They started going up in&nbsp;
October when Donald Trump was still president.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:35.920
And what we're seeing is demand for gasoline&nbsp;
recover as the pandemic starts to ease. It has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:42.560
nothing to do with Joe Biden. So serious media&nbsp;
should really just report this based on facts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:48.640
but without using the language that the right&nbsp;
uses. You know, when you talk about border crisis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:55.520
it's sort of like sleepy Joe in China virus. These&nbsp;
are terms that the right uses to frame the debate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:01.120
in a particular way where you're no longer&nbsp;
questioning whether there is a border crisis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:07.840
you're merely arguing as to whose fault it is&nbsp;
and to what degree it exists. And this is how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:14.960
the right does really well at framing issues. It&nbsp;
keeps Republican voters enraged. It doesn't really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:20.720
allow solutions to the problems, however. So&nbsp;
call it a predictable seasonal pattern that we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:29.840
observed for a decade, bolstered by the waning of&nbsp;
coronavirus to some degree and even none like what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:36.160
we even what we would call non right wing media&nbsp;
is using a lot of the terms of the right when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.720
talk about this. And as I've talked about before,&nbsp;
using their don't let them even set the agenda and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.200
narrative by using the language. And that's what&nbsp;
they successfully have done on so many issues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:50.880
for decades, as we've talked about with people&nbsp;
like George Lakoff and Thomas Frank here on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:57.360
program. So don't fall for it. Here's the data.&nbsp;
The data is clear and we're going to continue to&nbsp;&nbsp;

